---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About | JiApps">
  <main class="flex-grow flex flex-col items-center pt-24 pb-32 px-6 relative">
    
    <!-- Background pattern -->
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[linear-gradient(to_right,#8b8a891a_1px,transparent_1px),linear-gradient(to_bottom,#8b8a891a_1px,transparent_1px)] bg-[size:40px_40px] [mask-image:radial-gradient(ellipse_60%_50%_at_50%_0%,#000_70%,transparent_100%)] -z-10"></div>
    
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center space-y-8 mt-12 w-full">
      <h1 class="font-display text-6xl md:text-7xl font-extrabold text-ink tracking-tight">
        Building for the <br/>
        <span class="text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-600 to-brand-400">Indian retailer.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-ink-light font-body max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-16">
        JiApps was founded with a single mission: to provide fast, reliable, and affordable technology to businesses that have been ignored by Silicon Valley.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Our Story -->
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto w-full border border-border bg-surface p-12 rounded-3xl shadow-sm mt-12">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:font-bold prose-headings:text-ink prose-p:text-ink-light prose-strong:text-ink max-w-none">
        <h2>The Problem with Modern SaaS</h2>
        <p>
          Over the last decade, software has moved entirely to the cloud. While this works great for tech startups with gigabit internet, it's a nightmare for a busy garment store in a tier-2 Indian city. Network drops mean lost sales. Cloud databases mean recurring monthly "tax" just to access your own inventory.
        </p>
        
        <h2>The JiApps Approach</h2>
        <p>
          We believe in <strong>Offline-First Architecture</strong>. We build native applications that leverage the full power of your local hardware. Whether you're running our flagship POS system, BillZ, or our unified Accounts ecosystem, you can be certain that your software will work at the speed of light—with or without an internet connection.
        </p>
        
        <h2>Our Values</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Speed over everything:</strong> A checkout should take 2 seconds, not 20.</li>
          <li><strong>Data Sovereignty:</strong> Your data lives on your machine.</li>
          <li><strong>Zero Cloud Tax:</strong> We prefer fair, lifetime pricing models over endless subscriptions.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
